Requirement Analysis Phase

The Requirement Analysis Phase is the stage where we identify and understand what the users need from the project.

Main Points:

Collect Requirements – Gather requirements from users, teachers, students, or customers.
Understand User Needs – Find out what problems the system should solve.
Define Features – Decide the important functions and features of the system.
Check Feasibility – Make sure the requirements are technically and financially possible.
Prepare Requirement Document – Clearly record all requirements for development.
